1. Interface definitions under Direct3D/PyIdl/
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The modules under Direct3D/PyIdl/ are Python translations of the interface
definition files (.idl) distributed with the Microsoft Windows Software
Development Kit. Interface names, method names and signatures, structure layouts,
enumeration values and IID GUIDs originate from those files and remain the
property of Microsoft Corporation.

    Copyright (C) Microsoft Corporation. All rights reserved.

Translated from: Windows SDK 10.0.19041.0
Source files:    dxgi.idl, dxgi1_2.idl, dxgicommon.idl, dxgiformat.idl,
                 dxgitype.idl, dxgidebug.h, d3d11.idl, d3d11sdklayers.idl,
                 d3dcommon.idl

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Compiled shader blobs
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

VertexShader.py and PixelShader.py contain compiled DXBC bytecode built from the
HLSL shaders in Microsoft's DXGI desktop duplication sample. The HLSL source text
is embedded in the compiled blobs and carries:

    // THIS CODE AND INFORMATION IS PROVIDED "AS IS" WITHOUT WARRANTY OF
    // ANY KIND, EITHER EXPRESSED OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO
    // THE IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY AND/OR FITNESS FOR A
    // PARTICULAR PURPOSE.
    //
    // Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation. All rights reserved

Original sample:
https://github.com/microsoftarchive/msdn-code-gallery-microsoft/tree/master/Official%20Windows%20Platform%20Sample/DXGI%20desktop%20duplication%20sample

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. Structural inspiration
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The application-layer class structure (OutputManager, ThreadManager) follows the
C++ desktop duplication sample referenced above. SerpentAI/D3DShot was consulted
as a reference implementation:

    https://github.com/SerpentAI/D3DShot   (MIT License)
